{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ecs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ECS is an entity component system for Swift. It suits any program that updates many similar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"things each step, such as the bodies of a physics simulation or the characters of a game."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entities are lightweight handles. An ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","isActive":true},{"text":" holds no data of its own.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Components are plain value types, such as a position or a velocity, attached to entities."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"},{"type":"text","text":" holds the entities and their components, along with "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"resources"}]},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values the world holds once, such as a clock."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems are rules that read and change the world through queries and updates, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs them in the order you write, at the same time where they don’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conflict."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","isActive":true},{"text":" runs a world frame by frame, with a fixed timestep and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"states.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world is a copy-on-write value, like an array: copies are cheap and independent, so you can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keep one for a snapshot, an undo step or a rollback."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example, using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" components from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", spawns a ball and moves it one step by its velocity:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import ECS","","var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import ECS"},{"text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation, and you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"import one on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them in a declared order.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted"]},{"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"ECS"}],"role":"collection","title":"ECS","externalID":"ECS"},"references":{"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation","abstract":[{"text":"A world and its schedules by label, advanced one frame at a time.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Simulation"},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS","url":"\/documentation\/ecs","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them in a declared order."}],"title":"ECS","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule":{"title":"SimulationModule","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","abstract":[{"text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with states that switch systems on and off.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Store the state of a game or simulation as entities and components, and read and change it with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"queries, updates, and commands.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"WorldModule"},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS/GettingStarted":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Define components, spawn entities, and move them with systems that run in a schedule and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simulation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ecs\/gettingstarted","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Getting Started with ECS"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can.","type":"text"}],"title":"Schedule","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Systems"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","title":"World","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world","abstract":[{"text":"A collection of entities, the components they hold, and resources.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Entity":{"title":"Entity","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle that identifies one entity in a world."}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/entity","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"}}}